@page "/docs/guides/spa"
@layout DocsLayout
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

<PageTitle>SPA integration — Vaultex</PageTitle>

<div class="docs-eyebrow">Integration guide</div>
<h1>Single-page apps</h1>
<p class="docs-lead">
    Add Vaultex to a React, Vue, or Angular app. Browser-based clients use the OAuth 2.0
    Authorization Code flow with PKCE &mdash; no client secret involved.
</p>

<h2 id="register">1. Register a public client</h2>
<p>In the Vaultex admin portal, create a client with type <strong>SPA</strong>:</p>
<ul>
    <li>Client type: <code>Public</code></li>
    <li>Redirect URI: <code>https://yourapp.com/callback</code> (and <code>http://localhost:5173/callback</code> for dev)</li>
    <li>Allowed scopes: <code>openid profile email roles</code></li>
</ul>

<h2 id="react">2. React with <code>react-oidc-context</code></h2>

<div class="docs-codeblock">
    <div class="docs-codeblock-header">
        <span class="docs-codeblock-lang">Bash</span>
        <button class="docs-codeblock-copy" onclick="vxCopy(this)">Copy</button>
    </div>
<pre><code>npm install oidc-client-ts react-oidc-context</code></pre>
</div>

<div class="docs-codeblock">
    <div class="docs-codeblock-header">
        <span class="docs-codeblock-lang">tsx</span>
        <button class="docs-codeblock-copy" onclick="vxCopy(this)">Copy</button>
    </div>
<pre><code>// main.tsx
import { AuthProvider } from "react-oidc-context";
import { WebStorageStateStore } from "oidc-client-ts";

const oidcConfig = {
  authority:    "https://auth.vaultex.io",
  client_id:    "your-spa-client-id",
  redirect_uri: window.location.origin + "/callback",
  post_logout_redirect_uri: window.location.origin,
  response_type: "code",
  scope:         "openid profile email roles offline_access",
  userStore:     new WebStorageStateStore({ store: window.localStorage }),
};

ReactDOM.createRoot(document.getElementById("root")!).render(
  &lt;AuthProvider {...oidcConfig}&gt;
    &lt;App /&gt;
  &lt;/AuthProvider&gt;
);</code></pre>
</div>

<div class="docs-codeblock">
    <div class="docs-codeblock-header">
        <span class="docs-codeblock-lang">tsx</span>
        <button class="docs-codeblock-copy" onclick="vxCopy(this)">Copy</button>
    </div>
<pre><code>// App.tsx
import { useAuth } from "react-oidc-context";

export default function App() {
  const auth = useAuth();

  if (auth.isLoading)         return &lt;p&gt;Loading...&lt;/p&gt;;
  if (auth.error)             return &lt;p&gt;Error: {auth.error.message}&lt;/p&gt;;
  if (!auth.isAuthenticated)  return &lt;button onClick={() =&gt; auth.signinRedirect()}&gt;Sign in&lt;/button&gt;;

  return (
    &lt;div&gt;
      &lt;p&gt;Hello {auth.user?.profile.name}&lt;/p&gt;
      &lt;button onClick={() =&gt; auth.signoutRedirect()}&gt;Sign out&lt;/button&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
  );
}</code></pre>
</div>

<h2 id="api-calls">3. Calling your API</h2>
<p>Attach the access token to outgoing requests:</p>

<div class="docs-codeblock">
    <div class="docs-codeblock-header">
        <span class="docs-codeblock-lang">ts</span>
        <button class="docs-codeblock-copy" onclick="vxCopy(this)">Copy</button>
    </div>
<pre><code>const res = await fetch("/api/orders", {
  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${auth.user?.access_token}` },
});</code></pre>
</div>

<h2 id="callback">4. Callback page</h2>
<p>Add a route that the OIDC library uses to finish the sign-in:</p>

<div class="docs-codeblock">
    <div class="docs-codeblock-header">
        <span class="docs-codeblock-lang">tsx</span>
        <button class="docs-codeblock-copy" onclick="vxCopy(this)">Copy</button>
    </div>
<pre><code>// /callback route — the library handles parsing automatically
&lt;Route path="/callback" element={&lt;p&gt;Signing you in...&lt;/p&gt;} /&gt;</code></pre>
</div>

<div class="docs-callout docs-callout--warn">
    <span class="docs-callout-icon">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M1 21h22L12 2 1 21z"/></svg>
    </span>
    <div class="docs-callout-body">
        <div class="docs-callout-title">No client secret in browser code</div>
        <p>SPAs are public clients. Never embed a client secret &mdash; PKCE is what protects you. If you find yourself adding a secret, you've configured a confidential client by mistake.</p>
    </div>
</div>

